==Notes==
==='''General'''===
*Just like Talents and Ultra Talents, Talent Orbs only take effect for a unit's True/Ultra Form.
*Talent Orbs are not nullified by the Curse effect nor the [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]], except for Strong/Massive Damage/Tough Effect, which will be nullified by Curse as they are tied to the abilities themselves.
*When farming Orbs for NP, it is generally recommended to merge anything that isn't Rank D all the way up to S, as the resultant merged Orb either has the same total value of its constituents or could be sold for more. Rank D Orbs are the only exception and should be sold immediately, since a Rank C Orb still sells for the same 1 NP. To put this into perspective, a Rank S Orb has a sell value 25 NP and requires a total of either 18 Rank C Orbs or 36 Rank D Orbs, meaning merging Rank D Orbs will result in a massive loss of 11 NP.

==='''Effect Orbs'''===
*Defense Up and Tough Effect Up Orbs both reduce the amount of incoming damage taken according to the formula '''(100 - DT)%'''. The -damage taken bonuses stack additively with the same type of orb but multiplicatively across types. For S-Rank Orbs, as an example, two Defense Up Orbs give -40% damage taken and two Tough Effect Orbs give -50% damage taken, but a Defense Up and a Tough Effect Orb reduce incoming damage to (80% * 75%)x, which is effectively -40% damage taken (much like two Defense Up Orbs). The effect is also multiplicative with the Tough ability itself. (on Fruited traits, the -25% damage taken from an S-Rank Tough Effect Orb decreases incoming damage from 0.2x to 0.15x).
*The +attack multiplier from Massive Damage Up Orbs works by adding a flat bonus to the base Massive Damage multiplier. To calculate a unit's final damage accounting for Talent Orbs, the formula is '''(3 + AM)x''' without [[Fruit Treasures]], and it becomes '''(4 + AM)x''' with maxed Fruit Treasures. The multiplier bonus is so potent that even B-Rank Massive Damage Up Orbs are inherently more effective than S-Rank Attack Up Orbs at level 30, when both options are available. Furthermore, unlike Attack Up Orbs, the +attack multiplier scales with levels; at level 47, C-Rank Massive Damage Up Orbs also surpass S-Rank Attack Up Orbs.
**Strong Effect Up Orbs' +attack multiplier adds to the Strong Effect in a manner similar to Massive Damage Up Orbs—an S-Rank Strong Effect Orb takes a trait's Strong Effect attack multiplier of either 1.5x/1.8x and adds +.3 to it. The -damage taken from Strong Effect Orbs follows a manner similar to how Defense Up and Tough Effect Up Orbs work, being multiplicative with other -damage taken bonuses, including Defense Up Orbs and the damage reduction of the Strong Effect itself. (on Fruited traits, the -10% damage taken from an S-Rank Strong Effect Orb decreases incoming damage from 0.4x to 0.36x).
*To determine how much damage an Attack Up Orb will add to a given unit, go to the unit's article on this wiki, scroll down to "Stats", click "Detailed", click the "OFF" button next to "Stats Modifier", set Attack Treasure to 0, set the True Form/Ultra Form unit's level to 1+0, and multiply the attack stat displayed by 1 to 10 depending on the Orb's Rank in addition to how many are equipped.
*The bonus damage from Attack Up Orbs is a flat increase completely unaffected by all damage multipliers, including Weaken and even the 80% damage reduction applied to [[Mini-Wave]]s and [[Mini-Surge]]s. Technically, this means units with multi-level Mini-Surges (e.g., [[Talents|Talented]] [[Mola King (Uber Rare Cat)|Master of the Pacific]], Ultra Talented [[Coppermine (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Coppermine κ]]) as well as units with Explosions (e.g., [[Narita Kaihime (Uber Rare Cat)|Cleansing Flame Kaihime]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Talented Awakened Bahamut]]) can reap more benefit from Attack Up Talent Orbs than any other unit.
*For [[:Category:Multi-Hit Cats|multi-hit attackers]], the bonus damage from Attack Up Orbs is divided using the same formula as the multi-hit. For example, [[Nobiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Mystican Pasalan]] has an initial attack stat of 2,400, with a multi-hit attack that deals 50% damage on the first hit and 50% on the second hit; the result is that an Attack Up S Orb (initial attack stat x5) would add 6,000 damage to the first hit and 6,000 to the second hit for a total of 12,000 extra damage.
*Since Attack Up Orbs' buff doesn't scale with level, it effectively gives diminishing returns as its user is upgraded (e.g., a level 31 unit receives ''proportionally'' less benefit than one at level 30). This goes even more so for units reliant on damage-boosting abilities such as Strengthen or Massive Damage.
*Purchasable [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cats]] and [[:Category:Li'l Cats|Li'l Cats]] have very low initial stats, meaning  most of them gain only a minuscule amount of extra damage from Attack Up Orbs, especially those of lower Ranks.
*Strong/Massive Damage/Tough Orbs can only be used to improve the abilities of units against their existing targets. For example, [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazer]] can be given a Strong Effect Up: [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] or [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark]] Orb to make her pre-existing Strong Against Red/Dark ability even more effective, but she can't equip Strong Effect Up Orbs of other traits such as [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] or [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]].
*Massive Damage Up Orbs cannot be given to [[:Category:Cats with Insane Damage ability|units with Insane Damage]], and Tough Effect Up Orbs cannot be given to [[:Category:Cats with Insanely Tough ability|units with Insanely Tough]].
**Similarly, a unit with Insane Damage/Insanely Tough that gains it through Ultra Form will not gain any effect from a Massive Damage or Tough Orb equipped in its previous form in which said orb was compatible.

==='''Ability Orbs'''===
*Every other time a unit with an Orb that only activates on every second deployment finishes recharging, its icon will briefly flash and the Orb will appear on the upper-left corner of its icon, indicating that the next copy of the unit will have the Orb's effect.
*A Mini-Deathsurge will carry over any abilities that the Cat who created it had, including but not limited to [[Critical Hit]], [[Strengthen]] and [[Metal Killer]].
**Metal Killer will not receive the damage reduction normally applied to a Mini-Surge because it deals damage based on a percentage of the enemy's current health.
*Resist X Orbs stack additively with each other and their Talent counterparts, making it more effective to equip these Orbs on units with an existing Resist Talent of that type to make it a full immunity. For Wave/Surge/KB/Toxic, you need a S-Rank Orb for full immunity, and for every other effect you only need an A-Rank orb for full immunity.
**[[Urashima Taro (Uber Rare Cat)|King Gamereon]] is the only unit with a 70% Resist Knockback Talent, meaning he only needs an A-Rank Resist Knockback Orb in order to have full immunity to knockback. Likewise, [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] is the only unit with a 50% Resist Freeze Talent, meaning he needs an S-Rank Resist Freeze Orb to have full immunity.
**Note that Sage Slayer stacks multiplicatively with the Resist X abilities rather than additively, meaning Sage Slayer combined with an Orb won't give immunity to [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sages]]' debuffs.
*Boost Stories of Legend and Boost Uncanny Legends Orbs stack additively with a unit's existing Defense/Attack Buff Talents rather than multiplicatively, giving slightly diminishing returns on units with stat talents.
*Though the Shortened Cooldown Orb only affects every other unit, the reduced cooldown is applied to the cooldown of even-numbered spawns, making the unit's very first cooldown of the battle affected by the Orb.
*The Berserker Orb is unaffected by the boost that Strengthen [[Cat Combo]]s such as [[Macho Man (Combo)|Macho Man]] provide.

