==Trivia==
*The faintly visible flame symbol on Talent Orbs may be a reference to how 本能 ''Hon'nō'' (Instinct, the Japanese name of [[Talents]]) sounds similar to 炎 ''honoo'' (flame).
*Though having basic sprites in the game's files since [[Version 9.7 Update|Version 9.7]], [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] Talent Orbs are unused and can't be obtained through normal means.
**[[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] Talent Orbs were also present in the files as early as Version 9.7, but were unimplemented until [[Version 13.3 Update|Version 13.3]].
*Prior to [[Version 9.8 Update|Version 9.8]], only a few of the units with Talents could have Orbs given to them. The reason for this is unknown, as there was no clear criteria for who could and who couldn't. The specific units included:
**'''[[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]]''': [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]], [[Jurassic Cat (Rare Cat)|Catasaurus]], [[Thief Cat (Rare Cat)|Goemon Cat]], [[Fortune Teller Cat (Rare Cat)|Doctor Cat]], [[Witch Cat (Rare Cat)|Enchantress Cat]], [[Swordsman Cat (Rare Cat)|Elemental Duelist Cat]], [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Rodeo Cat]]
**'''[[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare]]''': [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], [[Bath Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Luxury Bath Cat]], [[Bodhisattva Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Tathagata Cat]], [[Cat Toaster (Super Rare Cat)|Catophone]]
**'''[[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare]]''': [[Ice Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Ice Crystal Cat]], [[Oda Nobunaga (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Nobunaga]], [[Takeda Shingen (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Shingen]], [[Windy (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Windy α]], [[Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Thundia β]], [[Megidora (Uber Rare Cat)|God-Emperor Megidora]], [[Sodom (Uber Rare Cat)|God-Emperor Sodom]], [[Princess Kaguya (Uber Rare Cat)|The Chaos Moon]]
*Prior to [[Version 11.4 Update|Version 11.4]], the Talent Orb Storage had the same interface as the Cat Storage and could only hold up to 128 Orbs at a time.
*Prior to [[Version 14.3 Update|Version 14.3]], only a few of the units with Ultra Talents could NOT have a second Orb given to them. The specific units included:
**[[Ice Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Ice Crystal Cat]], [[Megidora (Uber Rare Cat)|God-Emperor Megidora]], [[Raiden (Uber Rare Cat)|God-Emperor Raiden]], [[Mekako Saionji (Uber Rare Cat)|Mission Control Mekako]], [[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Mad Doctor Klay]], [[Thunder God Zeus (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Zeus]] and [[Sea Maiden Ruri (Uber Rare Cat)|Mer-Queen Ruri]].
*The filter's descriptions for Resist Slow and Resist Curse Orbs say, "Reduces damage from enemy Slow/Curse attacks," even though these effects don't cause damage. This may be a result of copying and pasting the Resist Toxic Orb's description without changing the word "damage".
*Resists Explosions' name is inconsistent with the other Resist Orbs/abilities, being the only one spelled as "Resists".

